<span class="text-content" data-text="best-in-slot-gear">
<div class="thumbnail-container">
<span aria-label="Icon" class="thumbnail" data-border-type="loud" data-size="small" role="img">
<span class="thumbnail-icon">
<img/></span></span></div>Best in Slot Gear</span></a></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class="markup-toc-wrapper exclude-units">
<button class="markup-toc-button">Show Table of Contents</button></div>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>As a <span class="icontiny" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif");'></span>
<span class="c1">Protection Warrior</span>, the nature of our gearing becomes ever complicated by our focus on different stats for different content. Before taking a look at the Best-in-Slot (BIS) gear listed below, I'd advise making yourself familiar with the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/classes/warrior/protection/tank-stat-priority-pve">Stat Priority</a> in Mists of Pandaria. <br/>
<br/>While we generally pursue <b>Parry</b> and <b>Dodge</b> as our main stats, they are neither the most defensive nor the most offensive stats in our toolkit, but offer a balanced approach that offers good offensive utility while not neglecting defense. Pursuing items with these stats also allows you to have 0 competition on loot, making the gearing process much easier. <br/>
<br/>There will be bosses in raids where you do not blindly want to pursue Parry and Dodge, however, and building appropriate sets for those bosses will be advised.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="pre-raid-best-in-slot">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_dungeon_gloryofthehero.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Pre-Raid Best in Slot for Protection Warrior</span></h2>This is an example of the Best in Slot gear available from all PvE sources available before entering a raid. While this gear may technically be the best available without raiding, it is unlikely that you will need all of these items before entering your first raid, and as you gain raid gear, your priorities will shift. Some of these options may be all but impossible to attain due to their low drop rate, such as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87545/inelava-spirit-of-inebriation">
<img alt="Inelava, Spirit of Inebriation" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_1h_pandung_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inelava, Spirit of Inebriation</span></a>, and alternatives for these can be found in sections below.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
